    "axis": "clarity",
    "evidence": "The headline, supporting sentence, metric cards, constrained-recall labels, and “Compare configurations” CTA establish the core claim and a next action across viewports. However, the charts are not self-explanatory: the PR curve has almost no usable x-axis labeling, the recall bars lack an explicit scale and on-bar values, and the ablation table mixes PR-AUC degradation with repeated “no change” D-recall results without clearly explaining the distinction. Dense jargon and very small mobile annotations further weaken standalone comprehension.",
